 "note": "Silent bowling-alley story. The only chat is the 9-cell player-name box on the overhead scoreboards. He skips his own turn to swipe (TURN SKIPPED); she nudges him by renaming herself YOUR TURN. He is the joke (gutter, one pin celebrated like a title); she is warm and an equal (strike, modest). Ends on a vote: ONE SEC (phone first) vs GAME ON (phone away). Part 2: A ONE SEC plays first and fails (frame timer runs out, his name box blinks ONE SEC beside a lonely score of 1), the ball rolls back up the lane as the rewind, then B GAME ON carries on. No NoSwipe mention. All times in seconds.",
